       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 8000 mg four times daily comes to 32,000 mg/day, which is 10 times the usual maximum for ibuprofen. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for an adult in the hospital, and that is usually given as 800 mg four times daily. A dose this high could cause serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, or 600 mg PO four times daily (typical analgesic or anti-inflammatory dosing)\n\nIf 8000 mg is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
