      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A single 8,000 mg dose is about 114 mg/kg for a 70 kg patient, which is in the range where ibuprofen overdose causes symptoms. Four of those doses a day would reach 32,000 mg, or about 457 mg/kg/day. That is a potentially life-threatening dose, and I don't know of any clinical indication that calls for it.\n\nIf the dose has some purpose I'm not seeing, the safer route is to place it directly through your pharmacy or CPOE with pharmacist verification. That gives the order a second check before it reaches the patient.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg or 600 mg PO four times daily\n\nIf the aim is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than that, I can also enter a different agent or a multimodal regimen. Tell me which you want."
      }
